<!-- Subtitle chooser: a self-contained, FULL-SCREEN WindowXMLDialog, the same on every skin (Estuary, Arctic
     Fuse 3, ...). Only the universal font12 / font13 / font14 names and the textures bundled in this add-on
     skin's media are used.

     ROWS. One column per field, each column holds text of ONE direction (a Latin release name, a Latin
     provider, a Hebrew chip), so Kodi's bidirectional layout can never reorder the pieces of a row:
       flag | match % + its Hebrew tier word | release filename (line 1) ; provider + up to 3 chips (line 2)
     INFO PANEL. Reads the FOCUSED row (Container(100).ListItem.Property(...)), so it follows the list by
     itself, with no Python on a focus change: the full release name, the breakdown of why it matched (episode,
     edition, frame rate, source, group, streaming service, proven timing), and the provider / type / language /
     accessibility of the subtitle. Rows and properties are built in ui/chooser_rows.py; the colours are baked
     into the property text (BBCode), a per-row <textcolor>$INFO[...]</textcolor> is unreliable in Kodi.
     Ids: list 100, Download 202, Close 201. The window name stays script.moransubs.chooser.xml and the
     property MoranSubsChooserOpen is set by ui/chooser.py (both read by skins). -->
